From: hackberrypiq20_kali
Subject: gpio: brcmstb: do not abort suspend when there is no parent IRQ

GIO_AON has no interrupt on the Raspberry Pi 5 and CM5 (the device tree removes it
because the firmware monitors the PMIC interrupt), so parent_irq is -ENOENT and
brcmstb_gpio_suspend() never sets priv->suspended. brcmstb_gpio_suspend_noirq()
then returns -EBUSY for "a wakeup source fired", and every system suspend fails with
"brcmstb-gpio 107d517c00.gpio: PM: failed to suspend noirq: error -16".
Only treat !suspended as a pending wakeup when there is a parent IRQ.
Seen on rpi-7.3.y 99dc5c58.

---
diff --git a/drivers/gpio/gpio-brcmstb.c b/drivers/gpio/gpio-brcmstb.c
index ad377619cf..9b198c77a6 100644
--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-brcmstb.c
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-brcmstb.c
@@ -584,8 +584,12 @@ static int brcmstb_gpio_suspend_noirq(struct device *dev)
 {
 	struct brcmstb_gpio_priv *priv = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
-	/* Catch any wakeup sources occurring between suspend and noirq */
-	if (!priv->suspended)
+	/* Catch any wakeup sources occurring between suspend and noirq. Only
+	 * meaningful when there is a parent IRQ: without one (GIO_AON on the
+	 * Raspberry Pi 5 and CM5) ->suspended is never set, so this would abort
+	 * every system suspend.
+	 */
+	if (priv->parent_irq > 0 && !priv->suspended)
 		return -EBUSY;
 
 	if (priv->parent_irq > 0)
